@@ -131,3 +131,21 @@ The choice should fall out of three cheap results, in this order:
 Then spike the front-runner, and record the result here whether it worked or not.

 **Deliberately unresolved and not to be resolved by drift:** whether the semantic layer is authoritative (B) or a projection (A/C). That is the actual bet of this project, and it deserves a stated decision on stated evidence rather than an accumulation of code that quietly settles it.
+
+---
+
+## Code exists now. It does not vote. — 2026-08-16
+
+[`../poc/`](../poc/README.md) is a Track B measurement instrument (→ D17, still open). **Nothing in it settles D11, and this section exists so that no future reader has to take that on trust.** Every choice it made that could have implied an architecture, and why it does not:
+
+| Choice in the testbed | Why it is not a vote |
+|---|---|
+| Records live in a local append-only file per party | §II.6's dependency (b) — "somewhere to put an append-only signed record" — is satisfiable under all four. A file is the smallest thing that satisfies it and is behind `AppendOnlyStore`, which is one class and one interface. |
+| `ChangeSet`, `Claim`, `Attestation` ids are content digests | §II.6's dependency (a). Native to **C**, available in **A** and **D**, expressible in **B**. It is a property of the *record*, not of where code lives. |
+| The channel is a Unix socket carrying NDJSON | Transport, and inventing transport is an explicit non-goal. Behind one module; the A2A binding replaces it wholesale. |
+| `NodeRef` is opaque bytes with an injected `covers()` | This is the *opposite* of a vote: it is built so Track B cannot express a preference about D4/D5, and a lint enforces it. |
+| TypeScript on Node | Group 3 of [`07-open-questions.md`](07-open-questions.md) defers the language until D11. It is a PoC-only choice, recorded there as such. |
+
+The one thing the run does bear on is **A's kill signal**, and only weakly. Under **A** the records bind to code solely through Track B's own store, which §II.6 already flags as "we have built documentation" arriving through a different door. The testbed's `Completion.witnessed_scope` is the field that would have to do that binding, and nothing here tests whether it can, because there is no code and no edits — only records. **That is a question for whoever spikes A, not evidence against it.**
+
+**D11 remains open.** The three cheap results the choice should fall out of are still W0, ~~W4~~ (done) and W9, and the testbed is none of them.
